\section{Fit statistics by model class}{
For each class of \code{\link[=table_regression_models]{table_regression_models()}}, the rows a one-model
table shows under the default \code{show_fit_stats} (Default), in their
order, then every token that gives a row when named (Available). A
parenthesis after a token gives the fits it is limited to. The change
tokens need
\code{nested = TRUE} and are not listed. The same lists are the columns
\code{fit_stats_default} and \code{fit_stats} of \code{\link[=table_regression_models]{table_regression_models()}}.

\if{latex}{\out{\raggedright{}}}\strong{Linear and generalized linear}
\itemize{
